## Getting started

1. **Install the toolchain.** [Devenv](https://devenv.sh/) (plus [Direnv](https://direnv.net/), recommended) gives you Task and everything else this project needs, pinned to known-good versions - see [Development Environment](development.md).

2. **Clone and enter the project:**

   ```shell
   git clone {{ repo_url }}
   cd {{ project_slug }}
   direnv allow
   ```

3. **Generate an SSH key pair** for provisioning access:

   ```shell
   task gen-ssh-key
   ```
{% if use_terraform %}

4. **Set up Terraform variables** for each environment - see [Secrets](secrets.md) for what goes where:

   ```shell
{% if use_staging_environment %}
   cp terraform/environments/staging/terraform.tfvars.example terraform/environments/staging/terraform.tfvars
{% endif %}
   cp terraform/environments/production/terraform.tfvars.example terraform/environments/production/terraform.tfvars
   ```
{% endif %}
{% if use_ansible and not use_terraform %}

4. **Fill in your inventory** - add your target host(s) to `ansible/inventory/<env>/hosts.ini`.
{% endif %}

5. **Run tasks.** This project uses [Task](https://taskfile.dev/) as its task runner. Run `task -l` to see everything available, or dig into [Managing Environments](environments.md) and [CI/CD](ci-cd.md) for the full workflow.

